  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-10T22:32:59.097Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a separated armature with a phys bone, which is attached to the bone(s) of another armature with position and rotation constraints. It's a pretty complicated setup, but I think this is reproducible with any setup where the phys bones get affected by a rotation constraint in one of its parents.\nThe phys bone doesn't seem to take the constraints into account correctly and end up in different positions than they should. This is especially evident when grabbing the phys bone, where it ends up being pulled in a completely different direction than where it should end up.\nThis set up previously worked fine with Dynamic Bones.\nCan provide a video upon request, if needed. Just wanted to get this reported asap.",
